contract=dict(status='SOURCE_ONLY_NEXT_TARGET_PROPOSAL_NOT_STATEMENT_SEALED_NOT_CLAIMED',one_minimal_next_delta='Construct a bounded positive REAL square root Gamma of full scalar D=I-T² on actual L2(nu), with the scalar energy identity for every u; internally consume compiled60 canonical complex lift.',provenance=dict(paper=paper,primary_snapshot=pin(ROOT/src['primary']['path']),license_note='Nonexclusive distribution metadata reused from immutable execution snapshot; frozen HTML has no literal nonexclusive-distrib substring. No new license validation/download/redistribution.',Mathlib=ml,Mathlib_license='Apache-2.0 per inspected file headers',Lean_toolchain=(ROOT/'lean-toolchain').read_text().strip(),scope='Source/API contract only. Root is sole next writer and must seal exact statement before proof search; current60 verification/integration remains separate.'),generic_header_contract=dict(proposed_name='AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareRoot.exists_positive_real_square_root',binders=['Omega arbitrary Type; MeasurableSpace Omega','mu:Measure Omega arbitrary','D:Lp(real,2,mu)->continuous_linear[real] Lp(real,2,mu)','hD:D.IsPositive'],conclusion='There exists Gamma:Lp(real,2,mu)->continuous_linear[real] Lp(real,2,mu) such that Gamma.IsPositive, Gamma*Gamma=D, and for EVERY u in the full real L2, norm(Gamma u)^2=inner(real)(D u,u).',internal_construction='Use existing60 for Dc/iota/R/Q/C. Produce complex CFC locally; Rc=CFC.sqrt Dc. Prove C Rc=Rc C internally, then Gamma=R o Rc.restrictScalars(real) o iota. No CFC/root/fixed-range-preservation/extension certificate is a public binder.',not_publicly_claimed=['Generic real uniqueness','All-real functional calculus','Specific joint Gamma_P','Centered inverse/polar']),actual_header_contract=dict(proposed_name='AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.RealDefectRoot.actual_positive_real_defect_root',source_binder_map=[dict(source='S1.p1/(1.1)',binder='Finite real Hilbert E with Borel structure/canonical volume; V ContDiff(real,2); NNReal alpha,beta,0<alpha<=beta; all x,v both global iterated-Frechet-Hessian bounds',adapter='Source R^d extended to finite real Hilbert/rank-zero; finite E does not imply finite L2.'),dict(source='2.6/2.7/B8/C1',binder='eta>0; actual mu=volume.tilted(-V), J=law(X,X+sqrt eta Z),nu=J.snd,Lambda=law(Y,2X-Y)',adapter='No probability/partition/integrability/kernel caller; original strong convexity derives them internally.'),dict(source='literal A2.Thmtheorem1.p1',binder='beta*eta<=1',adapter='Non-strict cap retains alpha*eta=1.')],conclusion='Under ONLY original displayed source hypotheses, probabilities mu/J/nu and genuine every-y normalized Markov S with Lambda.IsCondKernel S, Lambda.fst=Lambda.snd=nu; exists SAME scalar selfadjoint contractive mean-preserving T with nu-AE conditional action and positive D=typed I-T*T; exists positive bounded REAL Gamma with Gamma*Gamma=D and for EVERY u, norm(Gamma u)^2=norm(u)^2-norm(Tu)^2.',exact_same_identity='Reuse existing59/60 T. If59 norm-defect and60 genuine witnesses are separately destructured, identify S by the every-y normalized density and T via Lp.ext on their universal AE conditional actions; never replace with an abstract chosen contraction.',source_integrability='Parent55 supplies AE integrability of u and u² along S, parent59 probability/Lp-to-L1 and true disintegration preserve means. Every-y density is distinguished from per-u nu-AE observable equality.',test_consumer='After constructing actual scalar Gamma, existing55 squared microscopic defect yields norm(B(Mu))=norm(Gamma u) for every actual marginal u. This is a meaningful scalar/image precursor; the full printed all-macro object requires the adapter below.'),printed_macro_boundary=dict(source_B10='Gamma_P=(I_macro-UPP²)^(1/2) on H_P=ran(P), unique positive root, no eta prefactor, all macro functions including constants.',source_B11='UperpP* UperpP=Gamma_P² and norm(UperpP f)=norm(Gamma_P f) for EVERY f in H_P.',exact_joint_identity='With A=P U P and B=(I-P) U P, B*B=P U(I-P)U P=P-A² on the full joint space. The identity is I_macro-A_macro² ONLY after restriction to ran(P); writing I_joint-A² here is incorrect.',required_adapter=['SAME canonical M:u(y)->u o snd is an isometry with PM=M, MT=AM (55/59); actual58 production gives ran(M)=ran(P).','Build the onto isometric equivalence e:L2(nu)->ran(P) from canonical M, preserving all full-domain vectors; do not import centered sharp Tests just to obtain onto.','Transport Gamma to Gamma_P=e Gamma e^-1 and T to A_macro=e T e^-1; establish positivity and exact typed square I_macro-A_macro².','For printed first B11, identify the actual B_macro:ran(P)->ker(P) or its isometric joint inclusion and B_macro*B_macro=Gamma_P² from printed B5 joint block identity with actual selfadjoint orthogonal P and unitary involutive U.','Existing55 norm(B M u)²=normu²-normTu² plus scalar root energy already gives the norm identity on every M-image; onto M then supplies every source f. This does not alone prove the typed B*B operator identity or canonical root definition/uniqueness.']),separate_boundaries=dict(root_construction='The proposed next delta includes complex-root preservation and REAL descent because existence of a complex root alone does not produce the real operator.',complex_uniqueness='CFC.sqrt_unique is used internally to show C Rc C=Rc; no extra hypothesis and no new real uniqueness credit.',real_uniqueness='Can later lift any alternative positive real root and compare complex roots by sqrt_unique; requires explicit equality of lifted squares. Not included in the minimal existence/energy statement.',centered='Gamma q=0 follows energy and Dq=0; selfadjoint Gamma then preserves exact H0=ker(innerSL q). Restriction root of D0 is later integration; no caller centering premise.',order_inverse_polar='B15 Gamma0>=gamma I is not obtained merely by an injective norm lower bound. Needs a positive-root order adapter using actual delta/rho and production promotion of sharp Test consumers. B16 root inverse/polar remains distinct. Gamma0²=D0 IsUnit permits a bijective-operator route; generic left/right-unit factors require hypotheses and must not introduce DedekindFinite.',endpoint='alpha eta=1 means rho0/delta1 and T0=0,D0=I; keep this legal. Rank-zero E/H0 and infinite L2 must remain allowed. Full Gamma annihilates the constant q, so a full-space inverse is not claimed.'),route_at_most_7_steps=[dict(step=1,text='Consume existing60 positive complex lift for the given positive REAL D; retain canonical quotient maps and exact Dc formula.'),dict(step=2,text='Derive canonical C involution, conjugate-scalar action and antiunitary inner identity on complex L2 via AE scalar compLpL; derive R iota=I, norm/inner embedding identities without added inputs.'),dict(step=3,text='Construct complex normal CFC and real selfadjoint CFC internally on the COMPLEX operator algebra as in current Test; Rc=CFC.sqrt Dc is positive and Rc²=Dc.'),dict(step=4,text='Rebuild C Rc C as a bounded COMPLEX-linear positive operator, prove its square is Dc using C²=I and Dc C=C Dc; CFC.sqrt_unique gives C Rc C=Rc, hence Rc preserves Fix(C).'),dict(step=5,text='Define the bounded REAL map Gamma=R o Rc.restrictScalars(real) o iota. Use fixed range and embedding injectivity to prove iota Gamma=Rc iota, Gamma²=D and Gamma.IsPositive.'),dict(step=6,text='Use real selfadjointness plus apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_left to obtain generic normGamma(u)²=inner(Du,u); combine SAME59 defect energy to give actual normu²-normTu².'),dict(step=7,text='Instantiate under original PBPS binders with genuine S/T/D produced internally. Optional actual55 image-norm consumer demonstrates the B11 precursor; leave macro transport/operator identity and real uniqueness explicitly separate.')],false_or_circular_routes=['Do not equate pointwise conjugation C with operator adjoint; cfc_star only controls adjoints, not fixed-real-subspace preservation.','Do not compose REAL C with COMPLEX Rc without explicit scalar restriction and a complex-linearity reconstruction of C Rc C.','Do not assume a real CFC instance or use instStarOrderedRingRCLike to generate one from itself.','Do not use finite-dimensional real-Hilbert eigenbasis root formulas for possibly infinite-dimensional L2.','Do not silently access60 private/mangled providers as stable public APIs; use canonical maps and current public theorem, or independently seal a minimal public helper if truly needed.','Do not assume full T has norm<1; constants are fixed. Centered rho<1 is a distinct Test-only sharp consumer and cannot supply an all-macro open-ball root.','Do not label the scalar Gamma as printed joint/macro Gamma_P before the SAME M/onto/restricted P/U/B adapter is proved.'],failure_boundary='If antiunitary scalar transport or C Rc C positivity/complex-linearity cannot be established, stop at that exact adapter: publish its typed residual and compile-free diagnostic evidence; do not add it as a public source assumption or count a complex root as a real root. Root must statement-seal exact original target before implementation. No new SAU, Lean file, compiler, verification, decoder, canonical edit or completion granted.')
